# build artifacts
_build/

# vendored registry dependencies materialised by `moon update` / `moon add`, and
# by `moonx <target>` when the target is a registry coordinate (it runs
# `moon fetch`, which drops the package under `.repos/`).
# NOT ours to commit: it is a copy of someone else's published source, and
# `git add -A` will happily stage thousands of files of it. (Learned the hard
# way — a release commit once swept in the whole of moonbitlang/async.)
.mooncakes/
.repos/

# local formal-verification toolchain shims (machine-specific paths)
.why3.conf
cvc5wrap.ps1

# scratch logs from measurement runs (scan output dumps, big-tree timings).
# Evidence, not source: the numbers quoted in the docs are already recorded in
# EXTENSIONS.md, and these files are megabytes of per-file listing.
_qa/

# Measurement dumps written by the `_verify` gates: full per-file scan output and
# the gate-on/gate-off captures used to price a behaviour change. Evidence, not
# source — the numbers they produced are quoted in README.md, and each file is
# megabytes. `_verify` also holds the GATES themselves (.ps1), which ARE
# committed, so the ignore is deliberately narrow and only covers `_`-prefixed
# captures.
_verify/_*.txt
_verify/_*.json
# `remeasure.ps1` writes one full per-file scan per corpus into this directory,
# for the same reason and with the same size. It is NOT covered by the
# `_verify/_*.txt` rule above because that rule only matches files directly in
# `_verify`, not a subdirectory of it -- so `git add _verify` swept six
# megabyte dumps in before anyone noticed.
_verify/remeasure_out/
# Per-gate transcripts written by `Run-Gate` (release.ps1). One file per mutation
# gate, rewritten on every release run. Evidence, not source -- and it only exists
# BECAUSE the summary filter was hiding gate failures: a run that reports a gate
# FAILED now prints the path so the full text survives. Not covered by the
# `_verify/_*.txt` rule above for the same reason `remeasure_out` is not: `*` does
# not cross `/`, so a rule for files directly in `_verify` never matches a
# subdirectory of it. These are `.log` as well as nested, so both facts apply.
_verify/_gatelogs/

# The mooncakes credential. `git add -A` staged it once before .moonignore
# existed; the token inside is live. The copy CI needs is a GitHub Actions
# secret, not a file in the tree. .moonignore covers the publish side of this.
credentials.json
*.credentials.json
